cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this manuscript using the metadata below."
title: "Who Is Cloning My Repositories? A Case Study of Unusually Regular GitHub Traffic"
type: report
authors:
  - family-names: "McCoy"
    given-names: "Taylor"
date-released: 2026-10-20
version: 1.4.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/tmccoy678/Who-is-cloning-my-repos"
abstract: >-
  I investigated 8,372 GitHub-counted clone events across six public repositories
  in a 14-day window. Four repositories showed a narrow daily plateau in a
  retrospectively selected six-day interval. Reproducible reanalysis compares
  observation windows and count rates, screens 138 external series to retain 134,
  and replays all 138 original extracted vectors from pinned public sources.
  Recurring automated collection is a plausible explanation; the operator and
  causal mechanism remain unknown.
